; ==== the accumulator gains this block  and is multiplied by r ====
; The step itself is poly1305/absorb  pasted; what is left here is the glue
; that hands it its three operands and takes the accumulator back; absorb runs
; at @0x19e  which is past everything this file keeps  so nothing it touches
; overlaps r  s  the accumulator  the block or the counters;
;
; r is copied and not moved  because absorb consumes it and every later block
; needs it again; the copy goes to absorb's r slot and to a temp in one pass
; and the temp hands the original straight back;
; absorb hands its frame back empty  so this holds at the top of every block;
; It catches the glue LEAVING something behind: taking the accumulator home
; from the wrong cell strands seventeen bytes here  and the next block then
; adds them in; It does not catch a glue offset that merely lands wrong INSIDE
; the frame  since absorb consumes whatever is in there either way; the two
; block vectors are what catch that;
; ASSERT zero 414:717
